      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'm so sorry you're feeling this weight of erasure, especially when your friends still see \"us\" instead of just \"me.\" Sometimes the loudest silence in a relationship is hearing the world call you \"us\" while you feel completely afraid to answer. It's okay for your reality to differ from theirs until you can find a space where your individual experience is valid again.",
      "source": "target",
