      "content": "Your feelings of detachment and the logical exhaustion of \"pretending\" are valid responses to surviving something profound enough to reshape your entire sense of self. While it feels like the story has ended, do not mistake this finality for a permanent state of unfeeling or the absence of life shaping future experiences; even \"extra\" characters in a story can influence how the scene concludes. Please consider speaking with a therapist, as they can help process this grief of identity beyond sadness and support you in finding a path forward where you feel seen on your own terms.",
